{"name":"Link to the Past","hex":"#d2b48c","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"link","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A connection between places, people, events, things, or ideas.","One element of a chain or other connected series."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To connect (two or more things).","To contain a hyperlink to another page."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/link"},{"term":"past","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The period of time that has already happened, in contrast to the present and the future.","The past tense."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having already happened; in the past; finished. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","Following expressions of time to indicate how long ago something happened; ago."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/past"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past","blocks":[{"text":"The Legend of Zelda: A Link to the Past is a 1991 action-adventure game developed and published by Nintendo for the Super Nintendo Entertainment System (SNES). It is the third game in The Legend of Zelda series, following Zelda II: The Adventure of Link (1987). It was released in Japan in 1991, and in North America and Europe in 1992."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/2/21/The_Legend_of_Zelda_A_Link_to_the_Past_SNES_Game_Cover.jpg/330px-The_Legend_of_Zelda_A_Link_to_the_Past_SNES_Game_Cover.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Legend_of_Zelda%3A_A_Link_to_the_Past","wikidata":"Q370055"},{"title":"Link (The Legend of Zelda)","blocks":[{"text":"Link is a character and the protagonist of Nintendo's video game franchise The Legend of Zelda. He was created by Japanese video game designer Shigeru Miyamoto. Link was introduced as the hero of the original The Legend of Zelda video game in 1986 and has appeared in a total of 21 entries in the series, as well as a number of spin-offs. Common elements in the series include Link travelling through Hyrule whilst exploring dungeons, battling creatures, and solving puzzles until he eventually defeats the series' primary antagonist, Ganon, and saves Princess Zelda."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/9/9d/Link_%28Hyrule_Historia%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Link_(The_Legend_of_Zelda)","wikidata":"Q568553"},{"title":"Past","blocks":[{"text":"The past is the set of all events that occurred before a given point in time. The past is contrasted with and defined by the present and the future. The concept of the past is derived from the linear fashion in which human observers experience time, and is accessed through memory and recollection. In addition, humans have recorded the past since the advent of written language."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Bouncing_ball_strobe_edit.jpg/330px-Bouncing_ball_strobe_edit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Past","wikidata":"Q192630"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/62/Legend_of_Zelda_a_Link_to_the_Past_Screen02.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/62/Legend_of_Zelda_a_Link_to_the_Past_Screen02.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"Link can travel between two worlds, which have similar layouts but different aesthetics. Shown is the same location in the Light World (top) and the Dark World (bottom), a dilapidated parallel Hyrule.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALegend_of_Zelda_a_Link_to_the_Past_Screen02.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c7/Takashi_Tezuka_GDC_2024_2_%28